AB  - Corruption which means the abuse of the authority for the sake of self interest, even has different descriptions in different countries, affects all countries' balance of public revenue and public expenditure, tax system and also tax policies. One of the types of tax which has important place in tax system is corporate tax. The main objective of this study is to demonstrate the effect of corruption on corporate tax revenues. In this study, the relationship between corruption and corporate tax revenues is analyzed with system GMM method, using 16 OECD countries' yearly data for the period of 1996-2010. The results of this analysis show that lower levels of corruption lead to higher corporate tax revenues.
